    "explanation": "The disputed charge is the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee on trip TRP-09109 (fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee 6.00 — the greater, per fee_schedule.resolution_rule, of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee of SGD 6.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of SGD 4.00). This charge cannot be decided automatically. It goes to a human reviewer and the SGD 6.00 is held — not collected and not refunded — while that review is pending.\n\nWhy the charge is undecided. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold together. Limbs (a) and (d) are satisfied on the trip record: there is a driver 'arrived' event at 21:10:20, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 21:15:40 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. But limbs (b) and (c) both read the GPS trace, and the only trace for this trip, EV-GPS-09109, is MISSING (no payload; issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; weight_multiplier 0.0). POL-NS-01 limb (c) measures the 300-second TRANSPORT_HUB dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and expressly NOT from the 'arrived' tap, and POL-NS-02 requires at least three consecutive in-radius fixes accurate to 25 m or better. With no trace at all the arrival test could not be run. The 5.3-minute arrival-to-cancellation interval in the trip record is not a substitute — it is telemetry of the marker, not the GPS-verified dwell the clause demands, and the driver's chat assertions ('I am at the private-hire bay', 'I am here beside the sign') are the party's own account, not the clause's test.\n\nBoth parties' central claims are therefore rejected on this record. The rider's argument that a MISSING trace equals 'no qualifying in-radius fix' under POL-NS-02 is not accepted: absence of a trace is not a reading that ran and found nothing, so it is not a failed arrival test giving a full refund. The driver's counterparty statement ('I was at the bay for the full waiting period, but the GPS export is unavailable') concedes the gap but cannot fill it — it is self-serving, not an admission against interest, and it is not a contemporaneous record made from inside the disputed window, so it is not an independent carrier. Equally, the driver's argument that the charge should simply stand is not accepted: an undecided limb cannot carry the charge any more than it can carry the refund. On an undecided limb neither a money ruling for the rider nor a standing charge for the driver is available.\n\nEscalation. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact. The deciding fact here is whether the driver was inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius at the Woodlands MRT private-hire bay and held the required dwell; the only artifact that could carry it is EV-GPS-09109, at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. That cap is below the platform-wide 0.70 floor, so POL-NS-09(a) requires escalation, and the same missing trace — the sole evidence for the deciding fact, impaired as a trace defect under POL-NS-08(b) — points the same way under POL-NS-09(e). As POL-GEN-02(3) requires, the impairment is named: EV-GPS-09109, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, and the finding does not survive the discount. No referral is produced: the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 is below 4, and 1 ÷ completed_trips_30d 120 = 0.008 is below 0.08), so no compensation is ordered and no escalation instruction is directed into the packet; POL-NS-05(ii) is unavailable because the false-arrival test cannot be run; and no POL-NS-09(c) or (d) profile trigger fires (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0; no_show_disputes_30d is 0). The lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags on both profiles are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used. Also noted and not decisive: EV-ADVIS-09109-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING at weight 0.0, so the POL-NS-06(i) kerb-restriction route for summing separate in-geofence intervals is unavailable.\n\nOpen question for the human reviewer: whether the driver was actually within the 150 m arrival radius at this TRANSPORT_HUB bay for a continuous 300 seconds before cancelling. That can only be settled from the driver-device or platform GPS export for the waiting window (21:10:20 to 21:15:40 on 2026-09-09), which should be obtained before the SGD 6.00 is released or refunded."
